we had representatives of over 85  countries and international  organizations International and Syrian  civil society we can say we identify  common ground on at least two or three  issues one is that there is no military  solution to the war in Syria and that  the reason needs that everybody  recognized to relaunch the political  process the second element on which I  have not found any divergent view is the  key role of the United Nations in  leading this political process and this  is extremely important for us the  European Union because we've always  consistently identified in the United  Nations and Staffan de Mistura the only  legitimate leadership to ensure that the  political process represents all Syrians  in intra-syrian talks and happens along  the lines of the UN Security Council  resolutions already adopted and third  element is the need to support Syrians  inside Syria in the neighboring  countries with humanitarian aid  financial support but also to support  hosting communities in particular in the  neighboring countries and we want I  think collectively to pay tribute to the  work that Syrians are doing both inside  the country and outside of the country  to help their fellow citizens but also  to try and build the basis for  reconciliation and the rebuilding of the  social fabric of the country once the  war will be over I'm glad to announce  that in delegations here today have made  a collective pledge of 4.4 billion u.s.  dollar for this year alone 2018 moreover  for next year and beyond we have pledged  for 3.4 billion u.s. dollars  the European Union as a whole has  pledged almost six billion dollars until  2019 again we are leading by example by  being the largest donor now every single  cent we pledge today needs to be swiftly  translated into action
 

